some dreams are destined to be forever  more dreams  it's incredibly unlikely that i will  ever go to space  that i'll ever win a nobel prize or play  warhammer with henry cavill  but a dream that i have had for pretty  much my entire life  has come true and i can finally  tell you about it because after  two years or so of work i have  written a book i cannot begin to tell  you how happy i am to finally talk about  this i have i've  it's been two years of trying to keep  this huge project secret so first things  first i guess  what is the book what's it about well  it's not your typical youtuber book it's  not about me it's not an autobiography  it's not about youtube  it's about the thing that i'm most  passionate about which is  the earth's atmosphere now of course  there have been plenty of books that  have been written about the atmosphere  indirectly there are several behind me  there have been books that have been  written about weather prediction and  books that have been written about  climate change  but what i don't think has been done to  date is a book that explicitly is  about the atmosphere what it is  how it works and how we worked out  how it works because to me at least the  way that people discuss  weather prediction and the way they  discuss climate change you'd barely  think there was any overlap between  those two fields and yet of course  they both evolved out of the same tree  of knowledge of  atmospheric science and i want to really  stress  this is not a new science it's one of  the oldest branches of human knowledge  it goes back thousands of years  and over the course of its life it's  seen phenomenally interesting  individuals  and these fantastic riddles and  mysteries that perplexed people for  centuries  so the book is about the atmosphere but  more than that  something that i try to do on this  youtube channel and something that i  think typifies good science  communication  is to go beyond just the facts to focus  instead on  the methodology on the contextual  information that leads us to  an understanding in other words how we  worked out  how this stuff works so a fair part of  the book is about the  long arcs of history how science and  technology  and socio-economic factors interacted in  the past to bring us to our modern  understanding now if i was a publicist  this is what i tell you that this is the  book for you  if you breathe air which is that's a  large potential customer base but really  you should get this book if yeah you'd  like to learn a bit more about  weather prediction and climate science  and how we arrived at that modern level  of  knowledge but also if you'd like to  learn a bit more about how the big sky  thing above us  works which leads me to the name i  haven't told you the name yet the book  is called firmament the hidden science  of weather climate change and the air  that surrounds us  the reason for this title is that one of  the largest influences on me in this  project was it's right behind me  infinitesimal by amir alexander this is  a book about the historical development  of infinitesimal calculus  and when i read it it had a really big  effect on me partly because  it's one of the best examples of  historical science communication that  i've ever read  but also because of the simplicity of  the title combined with the imagery on  the front  i absolutely love how the two together  hearken back to this early modern  renaissance  concept of natural philosophy and  science as we  know it just starting to form and  so firmament was to me a natural choice  for this project to try and elicit that  same kind of feeling  firmament just being a very old word  originally from latin meaning  the sky and well that's kind of what the  book's about  wait what's that you want a title and  cover  fine okay this is what it's going to  look like  roughly it's nearly there we just need  to finalize it i'm delighted to say that  firmament is available to pre-order i've  just got goosebumps from starting that  sentence  i am delighted to say that firmament is  available to pre-order right now  there'll be a link down there in the  description and it will be out  on january 27th 2022.  i obviously think you should buy a copy  and pre-order one because i think it's a  really interesting book  but to sweeten the deal the lovely  people over at nebula which is the  educational streaming service that i  am on and also have a small role in  running unprompted by me  have said that if you pre-order a copy  and you email proof of purchase to this  email address  down here then they will give you a  month free  on nebula so there you go  added incentive but this is the time  that i now need to ask for your help  because whilst working on this project i  found that  i really like doing this kind of work i  love writing  and i love researching and getting to  really immerse myself  in things that i didn't know very much  about but  learned about from visiting places and  reading books and reading papers  and frankly i'd like to do this again  i have lots of ideas for other projects  that i'd like to write but  i'm not going to get an opportunity to  do those things unless  this book does really well at pre-order  because i'm a first-time author and that  pre-order response is going to send a  really strong signal to the publishers  about how viable this is as well  both as a book but also how viable i am  as an author so i asked the  publishers how many pre-orders did they  think would be a good  target to aim for and they said that 200  pre-orders in the first  week would be really really good so  obviously pre-order the book  if you would like to read it if you  think it sounds interesting but i'd ask  you if you're on the fence  and you'd like to support my work and  you'd like to give me a shot at doing  this again  and really get my kind of authorial  career as silly as that sounds to say  out loud  off the ground it would mean the world  to me  if you could pre-order a copy let's see  if we can  smash that 200 pre-order copies  in a week because i think we can do it  so just to quickly summarize  i've written a book no really i actually  have written a book  it's called firmament it's about the  atmosphere and it's going to be  available  on january 27th 2022 but you can  pre-order a copy right now at the link  in the description  now two things quickly just before i  finish off the video firstly  i'm sure that a lot of you will have  questions about this project that i  haven't answered in this video so i'm  going to be doing a q a live stream  tonight at 7 pm bst  on my twitch channel twitch.tv forward  slash dr simon clark  there is a google form down there in the  description lots of links in the  description today there is a link down  there in the description to a google  form where you can ask your questions  and we'll get through as many of them as  we can in the two hours that we have  booked in to do q a  incidentally if you didn't already know  i have a twitch channel where i  do some climate coding and study with me  streams and play video games and paint  warhammer  it's quite a mixed bag and secondly and  far more importantly  i want to say a huge thank you  to every single person who has supported  my work here on youtube  whether that's subscribing or watching  the videos or buying merch or supporting  me on patreon whatever it's been  thank you because if it wasn't for you  people  i wouldn't have this privilege this  opportunity  to to write a book and from  the bottom of my heart thank you so much  because you've made a childhood dream  come true  i i i don't know what to say other than  thank you thank you for believing in me  that's all for this video do join me on  twitch this evening  if you have some questions or if you'd  just like to learn more about the  project  and there will be more videos coming out  in the coming months sort of leading up  to the book's release where i'm  going to talk about the process of  writing it and researching and  also some stories that i didn't quite  have the  words space in the book to actually tell  in full but  i think deserve a youtube video on their  own but thank you so much for watching  again please do pre-order the book if  you'd like to read it of course or if  you'd like to support my ongoing work  down there in the description and  thank you i've said thank you so many  times but thank you again  i'll see you in the next one i'm gonna  be an author
 

